  "english": "3. Monday. Tone 3, 6th day [ԳՉԶ] of the Fast. Father/Hymn of the Youth [Հարց] Tone 8 [դկ]: \"Blessed are You, Lord God, blessed\" (Orhneal ter astuats orhneal).\n5. Wednesday. 4th day [ԴՉ] of the Fast. Eve of the Nativity of Christ.\nIn January:\n2. Sunday. Tone 4 [ԲԿ]. Sixth [day] of the Fast. Dismissal Hymn [Համբ.] Tone 4 [բկ]: \"The women anticipated\" (Kankhetsin kanaykn), to the end.\nSEVEN-DAY CYCLE OF THE ROMANS 4.\nIn January:\n6. MONDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The meat-eating period [between Epiphany and Great Fast] is thirty-four days.\n15. Thursday. [Feast] of John the Forerunner.\n17. Saturday. [Feast] of Patriarch Peter, Blaise, and the others.\n18. Sunday. First [Sunday after Epiphany]. Father/Hymn of the Youth [Հարց] Tone 7 [դձ]: \"The dawning of the Only-Begotten\" (Tsagumn miatsni).\n19. Monday. [Feast] of Anthony, and Triphon, Barsam, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n20. Tuesday. [Feast] of King Theodosius, and the Holy Infants of Ephesus.\n22. Thursday. [Feast] of Cyriacus and Julietta, and of Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Gregory.\n24. Saturday. [Feast] of the Patriarchs Athanasius and Cyril.\n25. Sunday. Second [Sunday]. Father/Hymn of the Youth [Հարց] Tone 5 [գձ]: \"Creator of all creatures\" (Ararichd araratsots).\n26. Monday. [Feast] of Vahan of Goghtn, and of Eugenia the virgin and her father, etc.\n27. Tuesday. [Feast] of Eugenius, Macarius, etc., and of Andrew the commander and his army, etc.\n29. Thursday. [Feast] of Adrian and his wife Anatolia, etc.\n31. Saturday. [Feast] of Gregory the Theologian. But know this, that when a leap year occurs, and the year-letter is [R], during this interval you shall not celebrate the feasts of Andrew the commander and Adrian, because they are celebrated in the last year-letter [R], after the tenth Sunday, as you see. Instead, on Monday celebrate Vahan, on Tuesday Eugenia the virgin, and on Thursday Eugenius. But in other years, celebrate them without doubt as they are set down here.\nIn February:\n1. Sunday. Third [Sunday]. Father/Hymn of the Youth [Հարց] Tone 6 [գկ]: \"Today with the heavenly ones\" (Aysor znd_nav). For the order of the following week, see the First Volume after Transfiguration [Vardavar].\n2. Monday. [Feast] of the Maccabees, Eleazar, and the others.\n3. Tuesday. [Feast] of the Twelve Prophets: Hosea, etc.\n5. Thursday. [Feast] of Sophia and her three daughters.\n7. Saturday. [Feast] of the Sons and Grandsons of the Enlightener.\n8. Sunday. Fourth [Sunday]. Eve of the Fast of Catechumens [Arachavorats].\n14. Saturday. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj].\n15. Sunday. Father/Hymn of the Youth [Հարց] Tone 8 [դկ]: \"Without beginning Word\" (Anskizbn band).\n16. Monday. [Feast] of the Atomian commanders, and of Sarkis and his son, etc.\nIn March:\n1. Sunday. Tone 8 [ԴԿ]. Great Lent Eve [Bun Barekendan]. See also the rest according to the order in the First Volume, from page 17 to Transfiguration [Vardavar], keeping the order of this place.",
